import Mathlib
import StacksProject_2024.Chap10.Lemma_10_70_2
import StacksProject_2024.Chap15.Definition_15_26_1
import StacksProject_2024.Chap15.Lemma_15_8_4

-- Declarations for this item will be appended below by the statement pipeline.

universe u v

noncomputable section

open scoped FittingIdeal
open scoped AffineBlowupChart

section

variable {R : Type u} [CommRing R]
variable {M : Type v} [AddCommGroup M] [Module R M] [Module.Finite R M]

/-
Domain-style sampling pass for Lemma 15.26.3.

Primary domain: affine blowup strict transforms and Fitting ideals of finite modules.

Sampled owner declarations:
* `Fit[R]_(k)(M)` from `Chap15/Definition_15_8_3.lean`;
* `fittingIdeal_baseChange` from `Chap15/Lemma_15_8_4.lean`;
* `affineBlowupChart_map_ideal_eq_span_singleton` from `Chap10/Lemma_10_70_2.lean`;
* `affineBlowupStrictTransform` from `Chap15/Definition_15_26_1.lean`.

Owner abstraction: this theorem is `source-facing`. Its ambient algebra is the Chapter 10 owner
`affineBlowupChart I a`, its module is the Chapter 15 owner `affineBlowupStrictTransform I a M`,
and the Fitting-ideal conclusion should be expressed through the canonical owner notation
`Fit[...]_(...)` rather than the raw `fittingIdeal` spelling.

Primitive data: the intrinsic ideal `I = Fit[R]_(k)(M)`, an element `a : I`, the blowup chart
`R[I / a]`, and the strict transform of `M` on that chart.
Derived API: the conclusion that the `k`th Fitting ideal of the strict transform is the unit ideal.

Source/core/bridge triage:
* `source-facing`: the strict-transform Fitting-ideal statement below;
* `core/canonical`: `Fit[R]_(k)(M)`, `affineBlowupChart`, `affineBlowupStrictTransform`;
* `bridge/view`: `fittingIdeal_baseChange` and
  `affineBlowupChart_map_ideal_eq_span_singleton`.
-/

-- Proof sketch: base change identifies the `k`th Fitting ideal of `M ⊗[R] R[Fit_k(M) / a]` with the
-- extension of `Fit_k(M)`, and Lemma `10.70.2` makes that extended ideal principal, generated by
-- `a`. Lemma `15.8.9` then shows that after quotienting by the strict-transform torsion, every
-- localization is generated by at most `k` elements, so Lemma `15.8.7` gives the unit Fitting
-- ideal.
/-- Lemma 15.26.3: if `a` is an element of the `k`th Fitting ideal of a finite `R`-module `M`,
then the quotient of the base change `R[Fit_k(M) / a] ⊗[R] M` by its `a`-power torsion, i.e. the
strict transform along the affine blowup `R[Fit_k(M) / a]`, has `k`th Fitting ideal equal to the
unit ideal. -/
theorem fittingIdeal_affineBlowupStrictTransform_eq_top (k : ℕ)
    (a : Fit[R]_(k)(M)) :
    let A := R[Fit[R]_(k)(M) / a]
    let M' := affineBlowupStrictTransform (Fit[R]_(k)(M)) a M
    Fit[A]_(k)(M') = ⊤ := sorry

end
